      "description": "Watch Heart Of Midlothian vs Dundee Utd highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. On August 9, 2026 , the Scottish Premiership delivered a high-stakes encounter as Heart of Midlothian hosted Dundee United . Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish their authority in a fixture that promised a tactical battle and plenty of goalmouth action. Explosive Start at Tynecastle The match ignited almost immediately as Heart of Midlothian looked to impose themselves from the opening whistle. It didn't take long for the deadlock to be broken; in just the 4th minute, Claudio Braga showcased his vision by providing a precise assist for Tom Renaud , who found the back of the net to give the home side an early advantage. The intensity remained high as Dundee United struggled to contain the pressure, leading to a yellow card for Daniel Bennie in the 11th minute. Moments later, the situation worsened for the visitors. Following a foul in the box, the referee pointed to the spot. Calvin Miller stepped up for Heart of Midlothian in the 12th minute and coolly converted the penalty, doubling the lead. The remainder of the first half was a feisty affair, characterized by physical duels that saw Amadou Ba-Sy and Lachlan Rose enter the referee’s book as both teams fought for control in the middle of the park. Braga Seals the Result The second half began with tactical adjustments, as Zachary Sapsford replaced Emmanuel Agyei for the hosts. Heart of Midlothian continued to dictate the tempo, and their persistence paid off in the 56th minute. This time, Sabah Kerjota turned provider, setting up Claudio Braga for a well-deserved goal, further cementing their authority on the pitch. As the clock ticked towards the final twenty minutes, Braga turned creator once again. In the 67th minute, he delivered his second assist of the afternoon, allowing Joshua McPake to strike and extend the lead even further. A flurry of substitutions followed for both Hearts and Dundee United , with players like James Wilson , Neil Farrugia , and Panutche Camara introduced to see out the game. Despite late efforts from the visitors, the home side remained disciplined until the final whistle blew at 90+4 minutes, securing a comprehensive victory."
